    {
      "id": "UgxSVJFry10Z9qxVk_d4AaABAg",
      "author": "@TheInvisibleLine-x9z",
      "authorImage": "https://yt3.ggpht.com/ytc/AIdro_mB0AEzuPBnHUnbJ05Kn6OFC0GWil99rk2mq0C8tMcOp8jSTPBxtIYFzdnOER1R9KYpvA=s48-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj",
      "text": "It's crazy how a straight line can take you almost around the entire planet! I never would have guessed the journey starts in Pakistan and ends in Russia. The part where it squeezes between Madagascar and Africa, then passes through the Drake Passage and avoids thousands of Pacific islands is mind-blowing. Geography never stops surprising me!",
      "likeCount": 0,
      "publishedAt": "2026-11-25T09:55:20Z",
      "replyCount": 0,
      "replies": []
    },
    {
